# .driveignore
# NOT a git mechanism. This documents what should be EXCLUDED if you mirror
# this folder into Google Drive (manually, via a sync script, or via
# Google Drive Desktop's selective sync / "Mirror files" exclusion rules).
#
# Why this file exists: .gitignore and .driveignore have DIFFERENT logic.
#   .secrets/.env -> git: EXCLUDE always   | drive: INCLUDE (drive is your secure channel)
#   .venv/         -> git: EXCLUDE          | drive: EXCLUDE (huge, regenerable, OS-specific)
#   .git/          -> git: n/a              | drive: EXCLUDE (binary churn, merge-conflicts Drive badly)
#   data/master/*.pkl -> git: EXCLUDE       | drive: INCLUDE (this is what you're sharing!)
#
# RECOMMENDED APPROACH (avoids "Drive Desktop mirrors local folder" entirely,
# which is the slow/flaky pattern you've hit before):
#
#   Do NOT point Google Drive Desktop at this project folder directly.
#   Instead, keep this folder purely local + git, and use ONE of:
#
#   (a) A scheduled robocopy/rsync job that pushes only the allow-listed
#       paths below into a SEPARATE Drive-mirrored folder
#       (e.g. G:\My Drive\{{PROJECT_NAME}}-share\), so Drive's sync engine
#       only ever sees a small, clean folder — never .venv, .git internals,
#       or caches.
#
#   (b) Manual "Add to Drive" of specific files/folders when you're ready
#       to share a checkpoint (lowest automation, but zero risk of Drive
#       choking on .venv churn).
#
#   (c) `gdrive` CLI / Drive API upload script (uv-managed) that uploads
#       the allow-listed paths on demand — see scripts/sync_to_drive.py
#       once Feature N needs it. Not built yet; add to spec.md as a
#       Core utility if you want this automated.
#
# ALLOW-LIST (only these go to Drive):
#   spec.md
#   PLAN.md
#   PROGRESS.md
#   ARCHITECTURE.md
#   README.md
#   .secrets/.env
#   requirements.txt
#   data/master/*.pkl
#   src/**/*.py
#   tests/**/*.py
#
# EXCLUDE (never to Drive):
#   .venv/
#   .git/
#   __pycache__/, *.pyc
#   .ruff_cache/, .pytest_cache/
#   .claude/hooks.log
#   raw/ (local scratch for raw project inputs, not backed up)
